        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cf1d76b9-d0f9-55b1-8211-d03d30798b4b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andy Fickman, Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price, Audrey Wells, Dwayne Johnson, H. Lee Peterson, Roselyn Sánchez\n- Companies: Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- Films: Pocahontas, The Game Plan, The Little Mermaid, Aladdin, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, The Prince and the Pauper, Rush Hour 2, Boat Trip, Act of Valor\n- Topics: film credits, editing roles, starring roles\n\nFacts:\n- Pocahontas is a 1995 American animated musical romantic-comedy-drama film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was an assistant editor for Walt Disney Pictures on The Little Mermaid.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Walt Disney Pictures on Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, and the Mickey Mouse short film The Prince and the Pauper.\n- Rush Hour 2, released in 2001, featured Roselyn Sánchez.\n- Boat Trip, released in 2002, featured Roselyn Sánchez.\n- The Game Plan is a 2007 American family comedy film directed by Andy Fickman, written by Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price, and Audrey Wells, and starring Dwayne Johnson.\n- The Game Plan was the last film in which Dwayne Johnson was billed using his ring name \"The Rock.\"\n- The Game Plan, released in 2007, featured Roselyn Sánchez.\n- Act of Valor, released in 2012, featured Roselyn Sánchez.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "88432aec-ce82-5b4c-8862-df20e947b1f2",
        "text": "Page: Pocahontas (1995 film). Sentence: Pocahontas is a 1995 American animated musical romantic-comedy-drama film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: The Game Plan (film). Sentence: The Game Plan is a 2007 American family comedy film directed by Andy Fickman and written by Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price and Audrey Wells and starring Dwayne \"The Rock\" Johnson (marking the last film in which Johnson uses his ring name \"The Rock\" in billing).\nPage: H. Lee Peterson. Sentence: His credits for Walt Disney Pictures include being an assistant editor for \"The Little Mermaid\", and the lead film editor for \"Aladdin\", \"Pocahontas\", \"Dinosaur\", \"Home on the Range\" and the short film \"The Prince and the Pauper; starring Mickey Mouse\".\nPage: Roselyn Sánchez. Sentence: In film, Sánchez has appeared in \"Rush Hour 2\" (2001), \"Boat Trip\" (2002), \"The Game Plan\" (2007), and \"Act of Valor\" (2012).",
